nitors; monitor errors say what failed","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"TeamHypersomnia/Hypersomnia","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-18T00:37:35Z","branch":"master","commit_sha":"ab75af33ebe5ea8bc768e048047fdcb546c90e9e","github_link":"https://github.com/TeamHypersomnia/Hypersomnia/commit/ab75af33ebe5ea8bc768e048047fdcb546c90e9e","commit_subject":"Bots with a sniper rifle (Hunter, Bulldup, Awka: invariants::gun::bot_aim_settle_secs 0.3) fire their first shot only after seeing the target that long - before, a hard bot killed at once. The settle drains over bot_aim_settle_drain_secs (1.5) after losing the target, so a quick re-peek waits shorter; easier bots settle longer and forget faster (x1 hard, x1.5 medium, x2 easy, x3 very easy). Outside combat, missions and buying, a bot with room for one more firearm runs for the nearest one lying within a screen around it (ai_behavior_retrieve_item, searched once a second spread by the bot's index, at once again when another bot grabs it first; an unreachable one is given up on) - e.g. on fy_iceworld, where nobody spawns in a buy zone. A map may limit which firearms the shop sells (game_modes.bomb_defusal.shop_allowed_firearms in its JSON, empty for all) - the buy menu, the server and the bots' purchases all follow it.","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"TeamHypersomnia/Hypersomnia","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-18T00:37:35Z","branch":"master","commit_sha":"9588a6aa68d7e94b107bdd434efad40b7fe7376c","github_link":"https://github.com/TeamHypersomnia/Hypersomnia/commit/9588a6aa68d7e94b107bdd434efad40b7fe7376c","commit_subject":"run-map skill: any map from the CLI for a test - run_map.sh (a dedicated server on an official, downloaded or edited map, BOTS=1, a spectator, visible or no client, KEEP=1, SERVER_EXTRA, LOG_GREP) and map_copy.py (a renamed copy with JSON edits), with the pitfalls hit: symlinked maps don't load, a copy named like an existing map is shadowed by it, bots play only with a human connected, PROGRESSIVE difficulty b